<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Containerized Node.js App with Docker & CircleCI'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Containerized Node.js App with Docker & CircleCI</h1>
  <p>Containerized a Node.js app with Docker and automated image builds and Docker Hub deployments through CircleCI CI/CD.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Docker</span><span>Node.js</span><span>CircleCI</span><span>CI/CD</span><span>Docker Hub</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/docker-circleci.png" alt="Docker CircleCI Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>containerizing a Node.js application</strong> using Docker and automating the build-and-publish workflow using <strong>CircleCI</strong>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Containerized a Node.js app using a <strong>Dockerfile</strong>.</li>
      <li>Built and ran Docker images locally to verify functionality.</li>
      <li>Pushed the Docker image to <strong>Docker Hub</strong>.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>CircleCI</strong> to automatically build and publish on every GitHub commit.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔄 CI/CD Flow</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — Source code, triggers CircleCI</li>
          <li><strong>CircleCI</strong> — Builds Docker image in cloud</li>
          <li><strong>Docker Hub</strong> — Container registry</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>📦 Container</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dockerfile</strong> — Defines the Node.js image</li>
          <li><strong>Docker Engine</strong> — Local dev and testing</li>
          <li><strong>EC2 / Cloud</strong> — Pull and run container</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Understood how <strong>Docker containers isolate</strong> applications and dependencies.</li>
      <li>Created and tested a <strong>Dockerfile</strong> to containerize Node.js.</li>
      <li>Published Docker images to <strong>Docker Hub</strong> for global accessibility.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>CircleCI for automated CI/CD</strong> — reduces manual deployment effort.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>In production, use <strong>Amazon ECS or Kubernetes</strong> for container orchestration.</li>
      <li>Store images in <strong>Amazon ECR</strong> instead of public Docker Hub.</li>
      <li>Manage secrets through <strong>CI/CD pipelines or AWS Secrets Manager</strong>.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>image tagging and versioning</strong> for deployment traceability.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

